Falsifies `system_tests::user::tenth_pass_map_gate_tests::the_pair_is_refused_through_page_frame_map_in_either_order` (claim 11).

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect: `PageFrame::MAP` records each page as read-only, whatever it maps, so the mapping
hold skips the check for it. That is a check that lives in `MAP_INTO`'s path alone: a page mapped
as code through `MAP_INTO` can then be mapped writable through `PageFrame::MAP`, and the page is
writable and executable in one space. The reverse order is still refused, because `MAP_INTO`'s
record reads the writable leaf `PageFrame::MAP` left.

Expected to fail: the assertion that `PageFrame::MAP` answers `NotPermitted`, reporting
`PageFrame::MAP mapped writable a frame the space maps as code`.

Replayed on 2026-10-31 (UTC) on aarch64 with `cargo xtask test --arch aarch64 --test
the_pair_is_refused_through_page_frame_map_in_either_order`: red at exactly that assertion.

